  "tagline": "Every block reads every signal.",
  "signals": "A block reads any signal as its own kind. A bit block reads a digit as 1 unless it's 0, and a wave as 1 while it's above the middle. A digit block reads a bit as 0 or 1, and a wave by its height, 0 at the bottom up to 9 at the top. A wave block reads a bit as the top for 1 and the bottom for 0, and a digit as a level, 0 at the bottom up to 9 at the top.",
